From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Benjamin Gregoire <Benjamin.Gregoire@inria.fr>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 17:25:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] From conditions on argument values to assertions on argument
 expressions

sc_to_eassert (safety_common.v) turns a safety_cond term on the argument
values into an assertion on the argument expressions: a predicate
IOpN_safety at the top becomes PappN_safety, any other condition the
expression sc_to_e builds. Outside the domain of the translation, that is
when the condition reads a variable beyond the arguments
(safety_cond_below) or has a predicate IOpN_safety below an operator
(safety_cond_expr), the assertion is false, which is sound. The conditions
wint_int builds are in the domain, so its assertions are unchanged.

safety_common_proof.v evaluates the conjunctions of assertions (aands) in
any mode and proves what check_xs buys: the conditions of the left values,
asserted before the assignment, evaluate to the same value after it
(check_scaP). safe_assertP relates a sequence of assertions run in one mode
to the empty command run in another. read_easserts_rec_E and
read_easserts_cons (expr_facts.v) compute the variables the assertions
read.

(cherry picked from commit 18c219977f7752a0044722f9d66627117cdd7c51)
